---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import markPortrait from '../../images/MarkPro.webp';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero-home">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Federal digital transformation / mission systems / applied AI</p>
      <h1><em>Business needs come first.</em> Then I figure out the technology, people, and investment needed to solve them.</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-aside" data-reveal>
      <p>I’m a GS-14 program manager and COR III at FDA. I work across strategy, architecture, acquisition, and delivery to push modern technology forward. That means proving it makes business sense to build it. Building my own products keeps me hands-on with the technology and close to the work of actually shipping something.</p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="/work/">See selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="mailto:mark@markgingrass.com">Discuss a role <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-rail" aria-label="Career at a glance">
    <div class="proof-grid">
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>20+</strong><span>Years in federal technology</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>400+</strong><span>Regulatory scientists served</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>GS-14</strong><span>Program leadership / COR III</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>15M+</strong><span>Records integrated in CIRDS</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading
        label="Operating range"
        title="Get rid of the buzzwords. I’m solving a real problem. Before spending money on technology, I look at what we can simplify, change, or stop doing altogether."
        body="I take mission priorities and connect them to the investment, acquisition, architecture, and product decisions needed to move forward. I know where those pieces overlap, where they get stuck, and who to bring together to get things done."
      />
      <div class="role-grid">
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Strategic direction</h3>
          <p>I set the direction, prioritize through both an enterprise and product owner lens, get the right people involved, and work with the team all the way through implementation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Technical judgment</h3>
          <p>I look past the technical solution itself, challenge the assumptions behind it, and connect the decisions back to the mission and business need.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Delivery accountability</h3>
          <p>I establish clear ownership, address problems early, and keep teams and vendors focused on building something that actually works for the people using it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Vendor leadership</h3>
          <p>I’ve led complex vendor environments for years, from onboarding new teams to coordinating multiple vendors, subcontractors, and projects running at the same time.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="project-stage tutorialrepo-flagship" aria-labelledby="tutorialrepo-title">
    <div class="flagship-shell">
      <div class="flagship-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="project-label">Flagship product / live on the App Store</p>
        <h3 id="tutorialrepo-title">TutorialRepo</h3>
        <p class="flagship-lede">I created TutorialRepo and took it from concept to the App Store. It is a real product, not a portfolio mockup.</p>
        <p>The app brings tutorials, practice, review, and progress tracking into one place. The first full course prepares learners for the AWS Solutions Architect Associate exam. I designed the product to support more courses without starting over each time.</p>
        <p>I direct the work end to end: product strategy, experience and content architecture, technical direction, subscriptions, AWS delivery, App Store releases, and the publishing system behind the content.</p>
        <div class="flagship-proof" aria-label="TutorialRepo product facts">
          <div><strong>Native iOS</strong><span>SwiftUI product</span></div>
          <div><strong>Subscription</strong><span>Commercial model</span></div>
          <div><strong>AWS</strong><span>Content + AI delivery</span></div>
          <div><strong>Live</strong><span>App Store distribution</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="button-row flagship-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="https://tutorialrepo.com/App" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the product <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/tutorialrepo/id6792567569" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View on the App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button link" href="/work/#tutorialrepo">Read the build brief <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flagship-media" data-reveal>
        <div class="flagship-video-wrap">
          <video autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload="metadata" poster="/media/tutorialrepo/home.webp" aria-label="TutorialRepo product demonstration">
            <source src="/media/tutorialrepo/app-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
        </div>
        <p class="flagship-caption">A 29-second look inside the working product.</p>
        <div class="flagship-screens" aria-label="TutorialRepo screens">
          <figure><img src="/media/tutorialrepo/home.webp" alt="TutorialRepo course home with readiness and review status" width="1284" height="2778" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/media/tutorialrepo/practice.webp" alt="TutorialRepo fingerprint practice screen" width="1284" height="2778" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/media/tutorialrepo/readiness.webp" alt="TutorialRepo readiness screen" width="1284" height="2778" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell case-grid">
      <div class="case-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Applied AI / inside the firewall</p>
        <h3>I use AI to speed up the work. Lean thinking decides what work is worth doing.</h3>
        <p>I orchestrate multiple agents across research, analysis, development, and decision-making to multiply what I can get done.</p>
        <p>I led the integration of an in-boundary LLM into CTP research tracking applications. It checks project abstracts against the coding manual, shows the evidence behind its recommendations, and flags disagreements. FDA reviewers make the final call.</p>
        <a class="button link" href="/work/#applied-ai">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-steps" data-reveal>
        <div class="case-step"><span>01</span><div><h4>Constrain the task</h4><p>Analyze against an authoritative manual—not an open-ended prompt.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>02</span><div><h4>Show the evidence</h4><p>Return supporting snippets and discrepancy flags with each recommendation.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>03</span><div><h4>Preserve accountability</h4><p>Use AI to narrow the discussion; keep decision authority with reviewers.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>04</span><div><h4>Fit the environment</h4><p>Operate within the agency boundary and the existing review process.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="identity-panel">
    <div class="portrait-wrap">
      <Image src={markPortrait} alt="Mark Gingrass in his home office" widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 42vw" loading="eager" />
    </div>
    <div class="identity-copy">
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label">The through-line</p>
        <blockquote>Solve the real problem.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Air Force veteran. Electrical engineering and computer science background. MBA. GS-14 program manager and COR III. I’ve spent more than 20 years in federal technology. I know how programs get stuck, how vendors drift, and how good technical decisions get lost. I expect technology investments to produce something useful and justify what they cost. I also know how to get the work moving again.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/profile/">More about how I operate <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading index="02" label="Field notes" title="Writing about systems, incentives, and the decisions between them." />
      <div class="writing-grid">
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">Federal IT</span><h3>The certificate warning nobody reads</h3><p>Read on Substack ↗</p>
        </a>
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">Applied AI</span><h3>The AI solution trap</h3><p>Read on Substack ↗</p>
        </a>
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">All dispatches</span><h3>Notes from the intersection of public mission and modern technology.</h3><p>Browse the newsletter ↗</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
